# Study of Network Devices and LAN Connectivity

## Aim

To study network devices and connect computers in a Local Area Network (LAN) using a switch, Ethernet cables, and IP configuration.

## IP Configuration

| Computer | IP Address   | Subnet Mask   |
| -------- | ------------ | ------------- |
| PC1      | 192.168.1.10 | 255.255.255.0 |
| PC2      | 192.168.1.11 | 255.255.255.0 |
| PC3      | 192.168.1.12 | 255.255.255.0 |

## Commands

### Check IP Configuration

bash
ipconfig


### Test PC1 to PC2

bash
ping 192.168.1.11


### Test PC1 to PC3

bash
ping 192.168.1.12


### Test PC2 to PC1

bash
ping 192.168.1.10

## Expected Output

text
Reply from 192.168.1.11: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=128

Ping statistics:
Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 4, Lost = 0 (0% loss)


## Result

The network devices were studied, and LAN connectivity between three computers was tested using the ping command.
